    {
      "id": "533898eb2f088ff6b25ed00c33c2a6440df86ff0",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1446435639,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Hi. I checked the change and I think we should change approach to transcoding in general...\n\nThe point is that when I wrote the code I didn't expected that rate can change in mid of RTP stream and I was obviously wrong. Your change fixes it, but just in case it changes once. If it happens two times in row, it breaks the rest of decode.\nExample: Try to manually select in RTP player Output Audio rate to something different than 8000 or 16000 (e.g. 44100 in my case) with sample of the issue. It initializes transcoder for G.711 and when coded changes to G.722, it do not change the transcoder and decoded audio is wrong.\nI think the code must remember source rate when transcoder was initiated and if it is changed, it must reinitialize the transcoder.\n\nI made proposal of the change.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7791033,
            "username": "j.novak",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "j.novak@netsystem.cz",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b98b9c10d87ea9f383019b704e727c94ba6895dd3c46291d23e400738e1c6f1d?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/j.novak"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-06-26T22:24:15.061Z",
